ank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T01:03:21-07:00","id":1078801,"title":"","content":"On the bottom of the pages, the word THE is listed before the word ANTHOLOGY - which is not the way that the title appears on the cover. On the cover it is simply ANTHOLOGY OF DREAMS, and on the inside of the book at the bottom of the pages, it appears as THE ANTHOLOGY OF DREAMS.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12375-wratticusq","name":"Wratticusq","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T02:24:41-07:00","id":1078810,"title":"","content":"Was thinking it was Talking about Shattered Dreams...<br /> <br /> But I backed Changeling too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-16T21:15:38-07:00","id":1079676,"title":"","content":"p. 100 &quot; 'Let's get just find her and get out of here...' &quot;<br /> <br /> Remove &quot;get&quot;. Should just be &quot;Let's just find her and get out of here...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T03:13:15-07:00","id":1081363,"title":"","content":"p. 6 (in Miss Opal's Clockwork Heart): &quot;was how Boggans expressed love.&quot; Boggans should not be spelled with a capital B. Kiths are never written with capital letters. So &quot;boggans&quot; (just like sluagh in the first paragraph on the same page).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-20T03:15:21-07:00","id":1081364,"title":"","content":"p. 52: &quot;Comtesse Lilianne Valadon de Beaumayne&quot;. House Beaumayn is spelled without the final &quot;e&quot;. Because it derives from the French Beau main (for belle main in reference to the founder).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-23T03:40:38-07:00","id":1082555,"title":"","content":"p. 75 (in the story &quot;Watercolors&quot;): the word &quot;Glamour&quot; is badly spelled (&quot;glamor&quot;), missing both a capital &quot;G&quot; and a &quot;u&quot; (as per the Irish spelling). Maybe the author's intent was to spell it as Sean heard it. Yet, since the dialogue is written, and since in the writing style the dialogues are not spelled to reflect the phonetic understanding, it seems to be a mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3747-mattboggan","name":"mattboggan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}